# Line endings must not be translated on the way to a working tree.
#
# `tests/golden.rs` compares generated text against these fixtures **byte for
# byte** — that is the whole point of the golden suite. Git's default on
# Windows is to convert LF to CRLF on checkout, which rewrites the fixture and
# fails `text_outputs_match_character_for_character` with a diff that is
# entirely invisible: the two strings print identically and differ in every
# line ending. It cost a CI run to find, so it is pinned here.
golden/** -text

# The emitted Lua is compared the same way and is read back in tests.
*.lua -text

# Belt and braces on the binary assets. Git detects these already; saying so
# means nobody has to rely on the detection.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.sd7 binary
*.smf binary
*.smt binary
